# Model and Artifact Locations

Perfume-Chem has one active generative-provider contract: the FastAPI backend
uses the OpenAI API. Codex development work runs through the signed-in
ChatGPT/Codex environment. The repository does not support an alternate local
or remote generative-provider fallback.

## OpenAI backend configuration

The two supported startup locations are:

- Repository-root `.env`: used by `python run_api_server.py`.
- `backend/.env`: used after changing into `backend/` and starting Uvicorn.

Create either untracked file from the repository-root `.env.example`. Do not
commit credentials. The active settings are:

- `AI_PROVIDER=openai`
- `OPENAI_API_KEY`: API credential supplied through the environment
- `OPENAI_MODEL`: OpenAI API model identifier
- `OPENAI_MAX_TOKENS` and `OPENAI_TEMPERATURE`: request defaults

Provider validation and runtime selection live in:

- [`backend/app/core/config.py`](../backend/app/core/config.py)
- [`backend/app/services/ai/factory.py`](../backend/app/services/ai/factory.py)

OpenAI model identifiers are provider-side identifiers, not files stored in
this repository. Consult the
[official OpenAI model catalog](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models)
before intentionally changing `OPENAI_MODEL`.

## Local non-generative model artifacts

The engine's semantic-search implementation is local and non-generative:

- Source: [`engine/knowledge/embeddings.py`](../engine/knowledge/embeddings.py)
- Embedding model: `sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2`
- Artifact directory: [`data/embeddings`](../data/embeddings)
- Primary index: `data/embeddings/knowledge_index.faiss`
- Numpy fallback: `data/embeddings/embeddings.npy`
- Metadata map: `data/embeddings/chunk_map.json`

The sentence-transformers package may populate its machine-level model cache
when the embedding model is first resolved. Those encoder weights and the
generated FAISS/Numpy artifacts are retrieval infrastructure; they are not a
chat model, reasoning provider, or scientific/sensory authority.

## Scientific ML and generated data

Numerical models, calibration artifacts, and learned scientific estimators in
the repository remain local computational evidence subject to their own
provenance and validation contracts. Their presence does not authorize a
generative-provider route and does not promote simulated or predicted values to
measured evidence.

Large generated artifacts and caches should remain outside Git unless a
specific repository contract requires a versioned artifact and provenance
receipt.

## Unsupported stale settings

Environment variables or files from earlier multi-provider or local-generative
experiments are unsupported. Current configuration fails closed to OpenAI; do
not restore a provider daemon, local generative weight path, alternate API key,
or fallback launcher from historical documentation.
